1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,537
Ravi makes the best chai in town.

2
00:00:02,837 --> 00:00:06,148
But one morning, a hundred
customers show up at once.

3
00:00:06,698 --> 00:00:09,151
Ravi tries to do everything himself.

4
00:00:09,451 --> 00:00:12,892
He boils the tea, takes the
money, and washes every cup.

5
00:00:13,192 --> 00:00:16,544
The line gets longer, and
angry customers walk away.

6
00:00:17,194 --> 00:00:19,583
Ravi does not need to work harder.

7
00:00:19,583 --> 00:00:21,024
He needs management.

8
00:00:21,724 --> 00:00:23,242
So, what is management?

9
00:00:23,543 --> 00:00:27,063
Management is the art of getting
things done through people.

10
00:00:27,663 --> 00:00:29,555
Ravi brings in a small team.

11
00:00:29,855 --> 00:00:31,288
Asha makes the tea.

12
00:00:31,288 --> 00:00:32,870
Kabir takes the money.

13
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:34,453
Meena washes the cups.

14
00:00:34,753 --> 00:00:38,196
Now everyone works toward
one goal: happy customers.

15
00:00:38,846 --> 00:00:40,993
A good manager wants two things.

16
00:00:41,343 --> 00:00:45,550
Effective means doing the right things,
like serving the chai people love.

17
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:50,725
Efficient means doing things right,
with no wasted milk and no wasted time.

18
00:00:51,075 --> 00:00:52,811
Great managers are both.

19
00:00:53,461 --> 00:00:56,872
To make this happen, every
manager follows five steps.

20
00:00:57,322 --> 00:00:58,222
Planning.

21
00:00:58,031 --> 00:01:01,827
Deciding what to do, like how
much milk to buy for tomorrow.

22
00:01:02,177 --> 00:01:03,077
Organizing.

23
00:01:02,995 --> 00:01:05,289
Deciding who does what, and where.

24
00:01:05,639 --> 00:01:06,539
Staffing.

25
00:01:06,408 --> 00:01:09,008
Finding the right person for each job.

26
00:01:09,358 --> 00:01:10,258
Directing.

27
00:01:10,251 --> 00:01:12,623
Guiding and motivating the team.

28
00:01:12,973 --> 00:01:13,993
And controlling.

29
00:01:13,993 --> 00:01:18,031
Checking that the chai still tastes
great, and fixing it if it doesn't.

30
00:01:18,681 --> 00:01:20,814
One week later, look at the difference.

31
00:01:21,114 --> 00:01:25,322
Ravi serves four times more customers,
and the wait drops from fifteen

32
00:01:25,322 --> 00:01:26,854
minutes to just three.

33
00:01:27,504 --> 00:01:29,996
And management is not only for business.

34
00:01:30,296 --> 00:01:33,227
Your school, your home, even
a cricket team needs it.

35
00:01:33,877 --> 00:01:34,811
Quick check.

36
00:01:34,811 --> 00:01:38,535
Ravi tastes one cup every hour
to make sure it is perfect.

37
00:01:38,535 --> 00:01:39,920
Which step is this?

38
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:42,720
Controlling!

39
00:01:42,708 --> 00:01:45,715
He checks the work, and
fixes problems early.

40
00:01:46,315 --> 00:01:47,324
So, remember.

41
00:01:47,624 --> 00:01:50,545
Management is getting
things done through people.

42
00:01:50,895 --> 00:01:52,793
Be effective, and be efficient.

43
00:01:53,143 --> 00:01:57,623
And follow five steps: plan,
organize, staff, direct, and control.

44
00:01:58,223 --> 00:02:03,079
Next time, we'll find out why every
organization in the world needs management.
